Portions of the Reddit Ads connector
(apps/backend/src/services/connectors/reddit-ads/) are derived from adport's
`packages/reddit` provider — specifically the Reddit Ads API v3 endpoint shapes,
the `{ data, pagination }` response envelope, and the exact-`next_url`
pagination contract.

MODIFICATIONS: rewritten for multi-tenant use. Tokens are resolved per tenant
through Zavi's Vault-backed getConnectorToken (with single-flight refresh)
rather than adport's local file-backed credential store and in-client refresh
loop; the write/mutation surface and the local policy engine were not ported;
an off-host pagination guard was added; errors were converted to Zavi's
ExpectedToolError contract.

Portions of the TikTok Ads connector
(apps/backend/src/services/connectors/tiktok-ads/) are derived from adport's
`packages/tiktok` provider — the Business API v1.3 endpoint shapes and field
names, and the three transport quirks (mandatory trailing slash, business
errors returned as HTTP 200 with a non-zero envelope `code`, JSON-encoded array
query params).

MODIFICATIONS: rewritten for multi-tenant use, per-tenant Vault-backed tokens.
The OAuth flow is NOT derived from adport, which has no OAuth implementation
(its CLI has the operator paste a portal-minted token); oauth.ts is first-party,
written against TikTok's published docs. The write/mutation surface was not
ported.

Portions of seven further ads connectors (2026-09-05) are derived from adport's
provider packages — endpoint paths, response envelopes, pagination contracts and
field names only:
  linkedin-ads/   ← packages/linkedin  (incl. the Rest.li encoder `restli()`)
  snapchat-ads/   ← packages/snapchat  (request_status / sub_request_status envelope)
  spotify-ads/    ← packages/spotify
  pinterest-ads/  ← packages/pinterest (bookmark pagination)
  microsoft-ads/  ← packages/microsoft (REST v13 paths, fault-object error shape,
                                        published sandbox developer token)
  x-ads/          ← packages/x         (Ads API v12 paths). The OAuth 1.0a signing
                                        in x-ads/oauth1.ts is first-party (node:crypto);
                                        adport uses the `oauth-1.0a` package.
  apple-ads/      ← packages/apple     (Platform API v1 paths, X-AP-Context header,
                                        and the ES256 client-secret JWT recipe in jwt.ts)

MODIFICATIONS, all seven: rewritten for multi-tenant use with per-tenant
Vault-backed credentials; OAuth flows re-based on Zavi's generic connector
scaffold (core/oauth2-authcode.ts) or bespoke routes; write/mutation surfaces
and adport's local policy engine not ported; errors converted to Zavi's
ExpectedToolError contract; vendor error bodies never echoed.

